<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ottoman–Venetian War (1570–1573)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1570–1573</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Fourth Ottoman–Venetian War, War of Cyprus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ottoman–Venetian War of 1570–1573 was fought between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> and the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>, allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-league-1571">Holy League</a>. The Ottomans conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a>, taking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicosia">Nicosia</a> in 1570 and Famagusta in 1571; the Holy League destroyed the Ottoman fleet at Lepanto in October 1571, but Venice made a separate peace in 1573 that ceded Cyprus.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ottoman-venetian-war-1570-1573.jpg" alt="Ottoman–Venetian War (1570–1573)" width="320" height="172" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unidentified painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Lepanto_1571.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
